## Results

The initial GPG encryption attempt failed following a passphrase-agent timeout. A subsequent attempt completed successfully.

GPG reported AES256.CFB encryption and successful decryption.

The original file and recovered working copy produced identical SHA-256 hashes.

## Investigative Assessment

The matching hashes establish that the decrypted file is byte-for-byte identical to the original file at the point of hashing.

The exercise demonstrates successful encrypted evidence storage and content-integrity verification. It does not independently prove the authenticity or completeness of the original acquisition.

## Limitations

- Original plaintext evidence remains unencrypted.
- Encryption does not replace chain-of-custody documentation.
- A separate checksum was generated for the encrypted artifact; its subsequent verification remains pending.
- Hardware and firmware identity of the Meshtastic device remain under investigation.

## Conclusion

The AES-256 encryption and decryption workflow was successfully completed. The decrypted artifact matched the original SHA-256 reference value, demonstrating preservation of file contents through the encryption and recovery process.
